WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.080
Brace yourselves, Guardians of the&nbsp;
Galaxy fans! Director James Gunn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.140
has a message that'll leave you&nbsp;
teary-eyed. His warning for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.260
third installment is cosmic - and&nbsp;
definitely worth a Groot or two.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:14.820
After years of anticipation, director James&nbsp;
Gunn and Marvel Studios have finally released&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:20.100
"Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3." The Marvel&nbsp;
Cinematic Universe's cosmic group first debuted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:26.460
in 2014, grossing over $333 million domestically,&nbsp;
emerging as one of the franchise's biggest hits.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.940
The current iteration of Guardians&nbsp;
is getting the swan-song treatment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:35.640
with "Vol.3" set to be their last ride. What can&nbsp;
fans expect from this final installment? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.220
lots of tears, according to director James Gunn.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.280
While speaking with Collider,&nbsp;
Gunn teased just how emotional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.880
the final film in the trilogy would&nbsp;
be. He set our expectations saying,

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:48.480
"I know that there's been a lot of people&nbsp;
crying in the screening, so I guess people cry."

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.560
Scared your favorite Guardian is going&nbsp;
to bite the dust? Don't worry — not all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:56.340
of "Vol. 3's" tears are the result&nbsp;
of sadness or grief. Gunn continued,

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:59.520
"But it's not all sad crying, there's&nbsp;
a lot of happy crying in the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:03.300
there's a lot of joy in the film. You&nbsp;
know, everybody talks about the emotion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.400
and it is emotional, but there's a lot of joy."

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.600
The film is packed with emotion, at least&nbsp;
according to Looper critic Audrey Fox,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.180
who praised the threequel for&nbsp;
integrating a heartbreaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:15.600
backstory for Rocket Raccoon.&nbsp;
Fox wrote in their 7/10 review,

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.580
"It does right by all of the characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:21.360
giving them the send-offs they deserve&nbsp;
— especially Rocket, who manages to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.200
evoke more of an emotional response than&nbsp;
his little CGI face has any right to."

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.760
Seeing as the threequel serves as a heartfelt&nbsp;
goodbye to our favorite group of intergalactic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:33.540
heroes, it more than makes sense that "Vol.&nbsp;
3" is the longest flick in the franchise.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:37.800
The latest film in the MCU follows the&nbsp;
Guardians on a chaotic mission that sees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:42.120
them racing against the clock to save one&nbsp;
of their own. "Vol. 3" notably features the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:46.140
reunion of Star-Lord and Gamora, who last shared&nbsp;
the screen together in "Avengers: Endgame."

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:50.280
For fans, "Guardians of the Galaxy&nbsp;
Vol. 3" is more than just a satisfying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:53.940
ending — it's a fitting and triumphant&nbsp;
send-off to some of Marvel's most quirky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:58.260
and colorful characters. Audiences gave&nbsp;
the film the much coveted A CinemaScore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:02.100
all but proving Gunn's still got the charm&nbsp;
and spectacle he had with the first film.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:05.280
"And we'll kill anyone who gets in our way."
"No, not kill anyone."&nbsp;

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.840
"Kill a few people."
"Kill no people."&nbsp;

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:10.860
"Kill one guy, one stupid guy who no one loves."
"Now you're just making it sad."

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:15.120
While Gunn and the rest of the crew are likely&nbsp;
basking in the film's positive reception, making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:19.260
the film was no small task for the creative.&nbsp;
The director admitted to The Toronto Sun,

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:22.860
"I was on edge the whole time I was&nbsp;
making this movie. I knew how difficult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:26.280
it was going to be to balance all of these&nbsp;
different characters and the final-ness of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:29.940
their stories in this trilogy. So it&nbsp;
was always an uneasy feeling for me."

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.160
Gunn seems to have knocked it out of the park,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:36.780
especially thanks to the film's extended&nbsp;
runtime. But how long exactly will audiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:39.240
get to spend with Star-Lord and the&nbsp;
rest of the gang this time around?

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:44.040
"Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3" clocks in at&nbsp;
2 hours and 30 minutes, making it one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:48.300
longest films in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.&nbsp;
It's also the longest film in the trilogy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:52.320
with "Vol. 1" and "2" coming in at 2 hours&nbsp;
and 1 minute and 2 hours and 16 minutes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:55.620
respectively. It makes sense that&nbsp;
"Vol. 3" is the longest of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:59.100
bunch considering it wraps up the&nbsp;
arcs first set up in the 2014 film.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:04.020
Prior to the film's release, Gunn made it clear&nbsp;
on Deadline's "Hero Nation" podcast that "Vol.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:08.520
3" would be the last flick in the franchise to&nbsp;
feature this current roster of heroes. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:12.360
it remains to be seen what the future holds for&nbsp;
the next generation of films in the franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:16.680
it's all but likely that "Vol. 3" serves as&nbsp;
Gunn's final Marvel outing now that he's head&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:21.120
honcho at DC Studios. Audiences are clearly&nbsp;
excited to see Gunn wrap up his trilogy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:25.800
with the film earning $114 million over its&nbsp;
opening weekend at the domestic box office.

